TITLE:: NdefRackBrowser
summary:: the module library down the left of the rack window
categories:: Libraries>NdefRack
related:: Classes/NdefRackGUI, Classes/NdefRackLib, Classes/NdefRack

DESCRIPTION::
A panel beside the rack listing every module of link::Classes/NdefRackLib::,
sorted and searched by name. The window makes one and frees it
(link::Classes/NdefRackGUI#-browser::); you do not make it yourself.

table::
## type in the search || only the modules whose names hold it, any case
## up, down (in the search) || move the mark along the names
## return (in the search) || make the marked module
## escape (in the search) || empty the search, the keys back to the rack
## click a heading || fold the modules under it, or show them
## double click a name || make the module in the first free spot of what is seen
## drag a name onto the rack || make it where you let go, its title under the mouse
## cmd-b, the toolbar's modules, < || fold the panel away, bring it back
## cmd-f || the panel shown, the search taking the keys
::

The sort is by category (OF's categories after the rest), by name, by rate -
audio or control, each module's SynthDef built in the language the first time,
a few a frame -, by the folder a module was loaded from, or the modules made
from the window most recently first. code::x2:: beside a name: two of them on
the rack.

It keeps no patch: the list is the library, read again when
link::Classes/NdefRackLib#*reload:: runs, and the counts are the window's
modules. Making a module goes through the window, exactly as its
strong::+ module:: menu does.

code::
NdefRack.gui;
NdefRackBrowser.sortBy = \name;     // for the next window
NdefRack.gui.browser.filter = "lp"; // the search, from code
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: shown
Whether the panel is shown; the window's link::Classes/NdefRackGUI#-showBrowser:: sets it, and a window opened again starts so.

METHOD:: sortBy
The sort a new window starts with: code::\category::, code::\name::, code::\rate::, code::\folder:: or code::\recent::.

METHOD:: width
The panel's width in pixels, read when a window is made.

METHOD:: recent
The library keys made from the window, the last first - at most 24, for this session.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/List::

METHOD:: noteUsed
Put a key at the head of link::#*recent::; the window calls it for every module it makes.
ARGUMENT:: key
a library key

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: view
The panel, in the window's layout.

METHOD:: field
The search field.

METHOD:: filter
What the list is narrowed to; setting it does not write the field.

METHOD:: sortBy
The sort shown; setting it sets the class's too.

METHOD:: rows
What is drawn, top to bottom: Events of code::type: \head:: (code::group::, code::title::, code::count::) or code::type: \module:: (code::key::, code::count::, code::side::).

METHOD:: keys
Every key listed under the sort and the search, folded ones too.

METHOD:: shownKeys
The keys drawn now, in order: what the arrows walk along.

METHOD:: current
The marked key.

METHOD:: fold
Fold a heading's modules away, or show them.
ARGUMENT:: group
a heading's code::group::, from link::#-rows::
ARGUMENT:: flag
true folds

METHOD:: isFolded
ARGUMENT:: group
a heading's code::group::

METHOD:: makeCurrent
Make the marked module in a free spot of what is seen.
